From 2f416963816c4f2c738a28b52e0ac5a145459720 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:14:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] audit3 H5: test_mt's terminal-window helpers in a
 TermView, the clean-machine checks in a Baseline

Each terminal-window test defined its own typ2, to0, tnum, mb, base, tv,
tb, wv, scr, tx, drawn, cxy, mv, btn, page and clip (typ2 five times,
tnum six, page and clip twice...); TermView(k) has them once, bound to
the same local names so the checks read as before. t_kill, t_park,
t_lcmd, t_exec and t_lists build back()/alone()/now() on a Baseline(k).
A test that boots a second machine binds its helpers again there (the
old lambdas followed the variable k); t_tpub's second machine now uses
its own MT segment where the lambdas used the first's (the same on
these boots). t_term's drawn() reads the view once, before: kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GRD5wiUMCniTFB6AGgxU9p
